# Folder Structure & DRY

## Directory layout (do not add parallel roots)

```
app/(app)/{feature}/page.tsx     ← thin Server Component (metadata + render client page)
app/(app)/{feature}/[id]/page.tsx ← thin wrapper only when route differs by context
app/api/{feature}/.../route.ts   ← Route Handlers only
components/{feature}/              ← feature UI (leads, sales, quotes, orders, crm, admin, layout, auth, public)
components/ui/                   ← shadcn + shared primitives (StatusPill, PhoneInput, …)
components/quotes/shared/        ← quote form building blocks (info-form, line-items-form, types)
components/quotes/quote-detail/  ← detail sub-sections (overview, history, skeleton)
lib/utils/                       ← pure helpers (format, ticket-math, compute-checkout, …)
lib/integrations/                ← email/SMS templates + send-* functions
lib/pdf/                         ← @react-pdf server components only
```

**Never** add page components back under `components/` root (e.g. `components/leads-page.tsx`). **Never** create a second detail component for the same ticket — use `QuoteDetail` with a `context` prop.

## Page → component pattern

```tsx
// app/(app)/orders/page.tsx — Server Component
import OrdersPage from "@/components/orders/orders-page";
export default function Page() { return <OrdersPage />; }
```

List pages live in `components/{feature}/{feature}-page.tsx`. Detail routes that share the same record use one client component:

| Route | Component | `context` |
|-------|-----------|-----------|
| `/quotes/[id]` | `QuoteDetail` | `"quote"` |
| `/orders/[id]` | `QuoteDetail` | `"order"` |
| `/payments/[id]` | `QuoteDetail` | `"payment"` |
| `/production/[id]` | `QuoteDetail` | `"production"` |
| `/completed/[id]` | `QuoteDetail` | `"completed"` |

New lifecycle stages → add a `context` + overview sub-component under `components/quotes/quote-detail/` or `components/orders/`, not a new `*-detail.tsx` page clone.

## DRY rules

1. **Helpers** — import from `lib/utils/*` (`format.ts`, `ticket-math.ts`, `invoice-payment-summary.ts`). Do not copy `relativeTime`, `fmtDate`, `parseLocalDate`, or currency formatters into components.
2. **Types** — shared shapes in `lib/types/index.ts` or `components/quotes/shared/types.ts`. Do not redefine `Ticket`-like interfaces in list pages when the API type exists.
3. **API logic** — one Route Handler per endpoint. Business rules (auto-release, evidence queue, paid-in-full) live in `lib/utils/` and are called from handlers — not duplicated in client components.
4. **UI blocks** — if the same card/section appears on 2+ detail contexts, extract to `ticket-overview-sections.tsx`, `*-detail-overview.tsx`, or `components/ui/`. Use `DetailCollapsibleSection` from `detail-layout-primitives.tsx` for long optional detail blocks (Timeline, Pricing, Payment settings).
5. **Tab counts** — dedicated `GET /api/{feature}/counts` per tabbed page (see `tab-counts` rule). Do not derive tab badges only from loaded list data.

## Before adding a new file

- Can this extend an existing component via props (`context`, `variant`)?
- Can this be a function in `lib/utils/` instead of a new component?
- Is the route a thin wrapper around an existing page component?
- Does the feature folder already exist (`components/orders/` for order-adjacent UI)?

If yes → extend; do not fork.
